# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/
/android/

# Export output
/build/
/export/

# Temp files (e.g. Assets/bars.png271044417.tmp)
*.tmp

# Reference photographs the backdrop art is derived from: ~45 MB of source images, several of
# them watermarked stock comps. Fine to hold locally and draw from, not something to redistribute
# in the repo or in a build -- the .gdignore beside them is what keeps Godot from importing them.
Assets/Area/references/**
!Assets/Area/references/.gdignore

# OS junk
.DS_Store
._*
__MACOSX/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Bought sound packs kept to pick from (564 MB); the sounds the game plays are the picks in
# Sounds/Selected/ and their cuts in Sounds/Sfx/. Until 2026-10-10 this rule was */Potential/*, which
# also hid every new file under Assets/Potential/ -- where tools/ cut the game's art from, so a clone
# needs all of it: nothing under Assets/Potential/ is ignored now but the one pack named below.
Sounds/Potential/*
# A bought pack no tool reads (67 MB), which the old rule was hiding. Track it or keep this line.
Assets/Potential/Other player characters/

# The viewport override tools/reels.py and tools/clip_video.py leave beside project.godot while they
# record (tools/recording.py). Godot reads it on every run, so it must never be committed.
/override.cfg
